WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.700
I played defensive end in college.

2
00:00:03.700 --> 00:00:06.220
I played on a unit called the Chinese Bandits.

3
00:00:06.220 --> 00:00:09.040
We were a defensive specialty unit.

4
00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:15.180
I played just a couple of handfuls of offensive plays when I was in school, but that was my job.

5
00:00:15.180 --> 00:00:18.960
One year I was a punter, part-time, only for one year.

6
00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:19.780
That was my position.

7
00:00:19.780 --> 00:00:24.400
You said that you played end, what kinds of skills does it take to play that position?

8
00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:32.060
A lot more than I had. [laughing] Oh, you’ve got to be . . . You have to have some quickness.

9
00:00:32.060 --> 00:00:36.500
You have to have the ability to stay on your feet and be able to move your feet a lot.

10
00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:39.640
You need some upper body strength to handle people.

11
00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:42.400
You had to have some good reactions.

12
00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:46.460
You had to be able to analyze certain situations, at least in those days you did.

13
00:00:46.460 --> 00:00:52.940
We not only had to protect on the run, we had to protect on passes as well, in certain situations.

14
00:00:52.940 --> 00:00:57.460
I don’t think I did a very good job at my position, but I lettered three years.

15
00:00:57.460 --> 00:00:59.480
I had some significant moments in my career.

16
00:00:59.480 --> 00:01:02.080
I really thought I was out of position.

17
00:01:02.080 --> 00:01:04.200
I really would rather have played offense.

18
00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:07.440
This is where I thought my strengths were, but there were some people that,

19
00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:12.100
apparently the coaches thought were ahead of me, and so I was put on defense.
